 "notes": "Lines on this map: block outlines are thin (2-3 px) lines closing each rectangular block of the Richmond grid; zoning borders are heavy (5-7 px) lines that run along the streets just beside a block's thin outline (e.g. x 706-714 beside the west edges of blocks 1444/1532/1555/1632 at x 717-725; x 615-629 in the Park-Presidio roadway; y 3510-3516 in Anza St under the south edges of 1534-1537; y 3713-3721 just north of the north edges of 1633-1637; x 1259-1265 P-box beside the west edge of 1538), or cut through blocks (y ~3350 in the Geary-Anza row, x ~1030 in 1535). I tell them apart by width: a block outline is the thin line, and every corner is on the outer (street) edge of that thin line; where a heavy line runs beside it the thin line is still visible next to it, and the heavy line is left in the street. Line positions were read off the 4x ruled close-ups and checked against dark-run profiles of page.png along rows and columns (outer edge of each thin run). Box chosen in the regular Richmond grid (Clement St to Cabrillo St, Park-Presidio Blvd to 2nd/3rd Ave) for its many heavy borders beside block outlines. The narrow blocks of Park-Presidio Blvd (14, 45, 15, 31, 15, 56, 16, 31) are typed as blocks: each has its own thin closed outline. Right-hand column (1438/1538/1549/1638) and bottom row (1632-1638) are cut by the box. Judgment calls: (1) the east edge of 1439 at its south end (x ~1251, y 3240-3286) and the east edge of 1553 (x ~977, y 3560-3700) and of 1550 (x ~1256, y 3680-3700) are hidden under heavy lines; typed straight through along the visible thin line above/below. (2) Heavy lettering ('P' at x 640-700, y 3440-3515; 'RH-1(D)', 'RH-1' etc.) sits over block outlines in places; outlines typed straight through the letters.",
 "drawn_by": "Claude (AI), 2026-11-23: by eye from ruled close-ups, each thin line's outer edge placed from dark-pixel run lengths read along rows and columns of the scan; checked on the labels picture"
